</header><div class="entry-content"><div class="wprm-recipe wprm-recipe-snippet wprm-recipe-template-snippet-basic"><a href="#recipe" data-recipe="7459" style="color: #333333;" class="wprm-recipe-jump wprm-recipe-link wprm-jump-to-recipe-shortcode wprm-block-text-normal">Jump to Recipe</a> - <a href="https://coffeecopycat.com/wprm_print/easy-homemade-eggnog" style="color: #333333;" class="wprm-recipe-print wprm-recipe-link wprm-print-recipe-shortcode wprm-block-text-normal" data-recipe-id="7459" data-template="" target="_blank" rel="nofollow">Print Recipe</a></div>
<p class="has-text-align-center">My rich, custardy, warmly spiced <strong>Homemade Eggnog</strong> recipe is a true holiday delight. If you’ve only ever had the store-bought stuff, you’re in for a very welcome surprise! Whether you serve it as is, spiked with booze, or sauced up with espresso, your Christmas is sure to be merrier with a batch of this beloved seasonal drink.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1800" data-pin-url="https://coffeecopycat.com/easy-homemade-eggnog/?tp_image_id=7455" data-pin-title="Easy Homemade Eggnog" src="https://coffeecopycat.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/HomemadeEggnog3-1200x1800-1.jpg" alt="closeup 45 degree angle shot of a clear glass of homemade eggnog topped with nutmeg and a whole star anise pod. " data-skip-lazy class="wp-image-7455" srcset="https://coffeecopycat.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/HomemadeEggnog3-1200x1800-1.jpg 1200w, https://coffeecopycat.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/HomemadeEggnog3-1200x1800-1-200x300.jpg 200w, https://coffeecopycat.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/HomemadeEggnog3-1200x1800-1-683x1024.jpg 683w, https://coffeecopycat.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/HomemadeEggnog3-1200x1800-1-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://coffeecopycat.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/HomemadeEggnog3-1200x1800-1-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://coffeecopycat.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/HomemadeEggnog3-1200x1800-1-720x1080.jpg 720w, https://coffeecopycat.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/HomemadeEggnog3-1200x1800-1-360x540.jpg 360w, https://coffeecopycat.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/HomemadeEggnog3-1200x1800-1-180x270.jpg 180w, https://coffeecopycat.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/HomemadeEggnog3-1200x1800-1-150x225.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></figure>    <div class="dpsp-email-save-this-tool " style="background-color: #c5f1de;">        <div class="hubbub-save-this-form-wrapper"><h3 class="hubbub-save-this-heading">Save This Recipe to Your Email!</h3><div class="hubbub-save-this-message"><p>We'll email this recipe to you, so you can come back to it later!</p></div><div class="hubbub-save-this-form-only-wrapper"><form name="hubbub-save-this-form" method="post" action="">                    <input type="text" name="hubbub-save-this-snare" class="hubbub-save-this-snare hubbub-block-save-this-snare" /><p class="hubbub-save-this-emailaddress-paragraph-wrapper"><input aria-label="Email Address" type="email" placeholder="Email Address" name="hubbub-save-this-emailaddress" value="" class="hubbub-block-save-this-text-control hubbub-save-this-emailaddress" required /></p><p class="hubbub-save-this-consent-paragraph-wrapper"><input type="checkbox" name="hubbub-save-this-consent" class="hubbub-save-this-consent" value="1" required /> <label for="hubbub-save-this-consent">I agree to be sent email.</label></p><p class="hubbub-save-this-submit-button-paragraph-wrapper"><input type="submit" style="background-color:#289e63;" value="Save It!" class="hubbub-block-save-this-submit-button" name="hubbub-block-save-this-submit-button" /></p><input type="hidden" name="hubbub-save-this-postid" class="hubbub-save-this-postid" value="7458" />                    <input type="hidden" name="hubbub-save-this-posturl" class="hubbub-save-this-posturl" value="https://coffeecopycat.com/easy-homemade-eggnog/" />                    <input type="hidden" name="hubbub-save-this-posttitle" class="hubbub-save-this-posttitle" value="Easy Homemade Eggnog" />                    <input type="hidden" name="hubbub-save-this-success-redirect-url" class="hubbub-save-this-success-redirect-url" value="" /></form>            </div></div>    </div></figure>



<p><a href="https://coffeecopycat.com/category/recipes/starbucks-copycat-recipes/starbucks-holiday-drinks/">Starbucks holiday drinks</a> are always top of mind during red cup season, but the sweetly spiced yumminess of homemade eggnog is a tradition that long predates the coffee giant. In fact, the first known mention of this festive elixir goes back to 1775! Even Starbucks can’t resist the timeless trend, offering an <a href="https://coffeecopycat.com/eggnog-latte-starbucks-copycat/">eggnog latte</a> alongside other Christmas drinks.</p>



<p>I can remember my grandparents making the best eggnog for Christmas Eve every year when I was growing up. They always kept the booze on the side so my sister and I could partake. Our thick, milky mustaches and sugar-fueled holiday glee are imprinted on my brain like it was just yesterday.</p>



<p>This cooked eggnog recipe is based on my grandma’s traditional recipe. It’s delightfully thick and creamy thanks to a hefty dose of egg yolks, whole milk, and heavy cream. The custardy consistency is like melted ice cream, making each glass as much a dessert as it is a drink. And the warm, cozy combo of cinnamon, nutmeg, vanilla and rum? Very merry, indeed!</p>


